{"complete":true,"city":"Suzhou","template_id":"global-first-24-hours","title":"Your First 24 Hours in Suzhou, Dealt as Cards","description":"A ten-stop first day that reads Suzhou through a surviving city gate, compact gardens, museum collections, canal-side streets, opera heritage, and an evening under Shantang’s lanterns.","icon":"schedule","cards":[{"entity_name":"Pan Gate","title":"Pan Gate","subtitle":"Daybreak orientation: read the old city at its southwest edge","notes":"Begin with the paired land and water gates. Their staggered arrangement shows how walls, roads, and canals once worked together as city infrastructure.","short_summary":"Suzhou’s preserved land-and-water gateway provides a concrete introduction to the ancient city’s defensive plan.","source_url":"https://english.suzhou.gov.cn/szsenglish/szcmyz/201611/915d8be121a54a288b229c2ba4c0c169.shtml","source_title":"Pan Gate_Ruins of Ancient City Gates","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Master-of-Nets Garden","title":"Master-of-Nets Garden","subtitle":"Morning scale lesson: see how much landscape fits into a small garden","notes":"Watch how the residence, central landscape, and western courtyard occupy distinct zones. The Peony Studio courtyard later inspired the Metropolitan Museum of Art’s Astor Court.","short_summary":"This compact garden pairs living quarters with a carefully compressed landscape composition.","source_url":"https://english.suzhou.gov.cn/szsenglish/sz4ajjq/201611/4fe3b02dec384dceb6789d453befe57f.shtml","source_title":"The Master-of-Nets Garden_4A Scenic Spots","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Pingjiang Road Historic Block","title":"Pingjiang Road Historic Block","subtitle":"Late-morning street reading: follow water beside the pavement","notes":"Use the surviving pattern—water parallel to land, river beside street—as your guide. Small bridges, waterside houses, and deep lanes make the block legible without a checklist.","short_summary":"Pingjiang Road preserves an urban pattern in which canal and street run side by side.","source_url":"https://english.suzhou.gov.cn/szsenglish/zglswhmjlm/201611/1ebe6f6827e14a10aabd5c9109e96e26.shtml","source_title":"Pingjiang Road_Cultural and Historic Streets","latitude":31.309589,"longitude":120.634804,"place_id":"ChIJO0cSBCenszURHGKud5-nq4Y","maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/place/?q=place_id:ChIJO0cSBCenszURHGKud5-nq4Y"},{"entity_name":"China Kunqu Opera Museum","title":"China Kunqu Opera Museum","subtitle":"Performance context: meet Kunqu through objects and documents","notes":"The museum occupies Quanjin Guild Hall and holds cultural relics, ancient books, and historical documents connected with Kunqu and other operatic traditions.","short_summary":"A specialist museum places Suzhou’s Kunqu heritage inside a historic guild-hall setting.","source_url":"https://english.suzhou.gov.cn/szsenglish/szzgkqbwg/201611/0e903486b37b422c83a9c7bc369abb83.shtml","source_title":"China Kunqu Opera Museum_China Kunqu Museum","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Suzhou Museum","title":"Suzhou Museum","subtitle":"Midday bridge: connect Wu material culture with modern architecture","notes":"Look beyond the I. M. Pei building to the museum’s four permanent exhibition strands. Their objects include bronzes, ceramics, jade, silk, embroidery, painting, and calligraphy.","short_summary":"I. M. Pei’s building frames collections devoted to the material and artistic culture of Wu.","source_url":"https://english.suzhou.gov.cn/szsenglish/bwg/201911/fdc603d3ae3040b89ef9b3ed071f8af1.shtml","source_title":"Suzhou Museum_Suzhou Museum","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Humble Administrator's Garden","title":"Humble Administrator's Garden","subtitle":"Afternoon centerpiece: study a garden as a sequence of environments","notes":"Notice the tonal change between sections rather than searching for one defining view. The eastern area was composed to evoke a rustic Jiangnan settlement.","short_summary":"The garden unfolds through contrasting sections, including an eastern landscape with a village-like Jiangnan character.","source_url":"https://english.suzhou.gov.cn/szsenglish/sjwhyclm/201611/0e774293426145f6b4b00d3a5717c6df.shtml","source_title":"The Humble Administrator’s Garden_World Cultural Heritage","latitude":31.324224,"longitude":120.62997,"place_id":"ChIJ95Kf4M-mszUREZWApzl39cg","maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/place/?q=place_id:ChIJ95Kf4M-mszUREZWApzl39cg"},{"entity_name":"Lion Grove Garden","title":"Lion Grove Garden","subtitle":"Rockeries in motion: trade the long view for winding paths","notes":"Here the route is the subject. Layered limestone rockeries contain caves and twisting stone paths, while corridors circle a central pool.","short_summary":"Lion Grove turns limestone rockeries, passages, and a central pool into a deliberately maze-like garden experience.","source_url":"https://english.suzhou.gov.cn/szsenglish/szyllm/201611/224608cf9755464587363e03fd9e6dd0.shtml","source_title":"The Lion Grove Garden_Classical Gardens","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Lingering Garden","title":"Lingering Garden","subtitle":"Late-afternoon counterpoint: watch architecture divide and reveal space","notes":"Follow the long corridor and note how halls, walls, doors, and turns partition the property. The garden is organized into central, eastern, western, and northern sections.","short_summary":"The Lingering Garden demonstrates how buildings and corridors can choreograph changing spatial views.","source_url":"https://english.suzhou.gov.cn/szsenglish/szyllm/201611/6a6c8bf51df742b4b3a1a56307437b21.shtml","source_title":"The Lingering Garden_Classical Gardens","latitude":31.3157066,"longitude":120.5925704,"place_id":"ChIJ9QCvWeagszURmzdDoPCfRw4","maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/place/?q=place_id:ChIJ9QCvWeagszURmzdDoPCfRw4"},{"entity_name":"Tiger Hill Scenic Spot","title":"Tiger Hill Scenic Spot","subtitle":"Day’s long view: widen the frame from gardens to terrain","notes":"Let the named features structure the visit: Sword Pond, Thousand People Rock, the Sword-Testing Rock, and the Verdurous Mountain Villa each tie terrain to the site’s recorded history.","short_summary":"Tiger Hill layers historic names and narratives onto rocks, springs, ponds, and built features.","source_url":"https://english.suzhou.gov.cn/szsenglish/sz5ajjq/201611/9b1909ce503e4597849ea06d8a755c1a.shtml","source_title":"The Tiger Hill Scenic Spot_5A Scenic Spots","latitude":31.33373,"longitude":120.579912,"place_id":"ChIJzR7WJgShszURNYYYQF05jFk","maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/place/?q=place_id:ChIJzR7WJgShszURNYYYQF05jFk"},{"entity_name":"Shantang Street","title":"Shantang Street","subtitle":"Evening close: return to the canal under red lanterns","notes":"End by tracing the street beside its river. Bridges, boats, whitewashed walls, and dark-tiled houses supply the structure; after dark, red lanterns change how those surfaces read.","short_summary":"Shantang Street closes the day with a canal-side streetscape recast by evening lantern light.","source_url":"https://english.suzhou.gov.cn/szsenglish/News/202509/b86991b450ad4bc79d364ffd4b30a8e9.shtml","source_title":"Beautiful night view of Shantang Street_News","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null}],"warnings":[]}
